{:id "0024-sound-cues"
 :title "Opt-in sound cues, synthesized, never alone"
 :lupa/deps #{"0022-polish-emphasis-contrast"}
 :lupa/area :flair
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "The 'audio flair' of the brief (You Don't Know Jack used sound to set
        the scene), done humanely: when the reader has turned sound on, an
        arriving message plays a short synthesized cue chosen by its
        delivery. Off by default, never autoplayed before the reader opts
        in, quiet, and always redundant with something visible
        (docs/research/conversation-design.md, principle 9)."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/sound.cljc" "test/halfahead/sound_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/core.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/core_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/fx/audio.cljs" "src/halfahead/app.cljs"]
 :design "halfahead.sound (.cljc, pure): (cue message) -> a cue as data,
          {:notes [{:hz n :ms d :at-ms t :gain g} ...]}, or nil for :plain.
          A distinct short figure per delivery: :headline a two-note rising
          sting (the game-show card); :typed a soft tick; :aside one low
          quiet note; :credits a three-note falling coda. Every cue lasts
          at most 600 ms, gain at most 0.15.
          Core: when :prefs :sound? is true and a NEW message starts
          performing (not initial history, not replay, not the reader's own
          message), handle returns the effect [:fx/play-cue cue]. Never when
          sound is off.
          Views: the Sound checkbox loses '(soon)'; label 'Sound'.
          halfahead.fx.audio (.cljs, the only Web Audio code): plays a cue
          with an AudioContext created lazily on the first cue after the
          reader turned sound on (a user gesture), oscillators and gain
          envelopes; never throws to the caller.
          app.cljs: route :fx/play-cue to fx.audio (alongside the Firebase
          effects); nothing else changes there."
 :acceptance
 ["sound/cue: nil for :plain; a valid cue for each other delivery, each at
   most 600 ms long with every gain <= 0.15 (tests, including a property
   over generated messages)"
  "Core: with sound off, receiving a new agent message yields no
   :fx/play-cue; with sound on, a new agent :headline message yields
   exactly one; initial history, replay, and the reader's own sent message
   yield none (tests)"
  "Views: the sound checkbox is labelled 'Sound' and toggles as before"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["No audio files or assets; no music; no voice"
  "Do not edit the schema, perform, the worker, or fx/firebase"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/research/conversation-design.md" "src/halfahead/app/core.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "src/halfahead/app.cljs" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
